# Member Contract

## Purpose

> **Scope:** The behavior contract shared by every member skill of this collection.
> **Key items:** bare activation, shared procedure filenames, update check, review modes,
> repository conventions, member-owned variance.

{{membership-contract}}

A member's own `AGENTS.md` and `SKILL.md` stay authoritative for that member - when this
file and a member disagree, the member's documents win and the disagreement is either a
recorded variance or drift that the member's own review resolves.

## Activation

Every member answers a bare `use <member>` request through `process/skill-activation.md` -
the same filename in every member. The procedure carries the same section skeleton:
Purpose, When This Applies, Procedure, Enablement Response, What Does Not Apply, and
Relation To The Modes.

The bare activation is informational standby: it reports the skill's name, version, and
operation roster, then waits for the named task - it never resumes plans, edits, or runs
operations on assumption.

## Update Check

Every member runs its `scripts/check-update.py` once per session, before any other step
of a loaded skill, and never repeats it within the session.

The check reports the upstream tip as a full `tip_sha` commit hash plus `tip_date`. The
update path applies that reported commit with `git merge --ff-only <tip_sha>` - gated on
the reported state (`ahead=0`, `dirty=no`) - then re-reads `SKILL.md` and any loaded rule
files. The merge fast-forwards to the reported `tip_sha`, never a later tip, and applies
upstream content without cryptographic verification - the trust anchor is the
remote-tracking ref the `tip_sha` was reported from.

A member on a detached HEAD reports `NO-UPSTREAM`. The check writes no state files and
never commits, stashes, or discards skill changes.

{{membership-update}}

## Shared Procedures

Five procedure filenames are shared across every member's `process/` directory:

| File                            | Role                                                     |
|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| `process/skill-activation.md`   | Bare-activation standby procedure                        |
| `process/json-exchange.md`      | JSON parameter exchange format                           |
| `process/operation-timing.md`   | Elapsed-time report for named request modes              |
| `process/session-review.md`     | Member session review the collection delegates to        |
| `process/operations-catalog.md` | Full operations table for "list all operations" requests |

A member may carry additional procedures beside them - the shared filenames exist so the
collection and cross-member maintenance can locate the common surface by name.

## Review Modes

Every member's session review accepts the same two flags:

- `autonomous` - also `automatic`, `unattended`, or `non-interactive` - resolves every
  review gate to the recommended option and reports each resolution inline. It never
  commits.
- `verbose` - reports the full option list and the rationale at every surface.

The collection's own session review passes both flags down to every delegated member
review.

Members generated through Forge additionally document `fully autonomous` in
`process/decision-modes.md` - zero question surfaces with safe skipping and partial
reporting - and the collection forwards that flag unchanged.

## Repository Conventions

- `AGENTS.md` is the agent-facing maintenance entry point. `SKILL.md` is the runtime
  contract and carries frontmatter `name`, `description`, and `metadata.version`.
- `evals/evals.json` holds behavioral regression prompts. Routing and gate changes
  extend it.
- A gitignored `work/` directory holds local artifacts. Shipped files never reference it.
- A change set bumps the member's version at most once between commits. The cadence and
  numbering format follow the member's own versioning document.
- The agent never commits automatically - it proposes a one-sentence commit message and
  leaves the commit to the user.
- Prose prefers a comma or period between clauses. A spaced hyphen marks an aside or a
  definitional separator, never a clause join.
- Findings and shipped examples stay anonymized - no real names, paths, or project
  identifiers supplied with a request.

## Member-Owned Variance

Variance is legitimate when the member's own documents record it.

A member that gains or changes a shared-contract surface keeps the shared semantics - new
variance is recorded in the member's own documents and reported to the collection's
session review, which updates this file.

## Relation To The Collection

`process/session-review.md` partitions lessons by owner and delegates member lessons to
each member's `process/session-review.md` - this file is the shared baseline that the
delegation relies on, and it overrides nothing inside a member.

The index may load several members on one task - each member still runs only its own
procedures and never reaches into a sibling's directory, so a member's documents assume
nothing about which siblings are active beside it.
